      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two things missing on the state pages this takes from the host, and I am raising them here rather than on the HVC patch because this is the function that consumes them.\n\nits_state and shadow are never checked for page alignment. hyp_virt_to_pfn truncates to the containing page and the BUILD_BUG_ON only bounds the struct size, not the offset it starts at, so a pointer near the end of a page leaves the host owning the tail. For its_priv_state that includes base, which the register handlers use as the MMIO address.\n\nAnd neither page is zeroed at EL2. __pkvm_host_donate_hyp re-maps and flips the owner but leaves the contents, so used_device_id_mask, device_id[] and tracked_pfns[] are all whatever the host wrote. used_device_id_mask \u003d U64_MAX makes the first track_device_id_add return -EINVAL and stalls the emulated queue.\n\nThe redistributor side has both of the same problems, so it is probably one helper.",
      "revId": "8d9ca225dc214be92a6887c0e63a59cddc47e42f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
