      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T13:58:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I ran into the problem you are mentioning and it was solved another way. However I think we are running into a question when hypervisor no longer trusts host (I think at this time it still does). \n\nRegarding the `reg-\u003epriv` states on the other end of the hvc both ITS state and GICR state are allocated with `__get_free_page(GFP_ATOMIC | __GFP_ZERO);`. Of course we can introduce a helper function like \n\n```\nstatic int donate_and_clear_host_page(void *addr)\n{\n\tint ret;\n\n\tif (!PAGE_ALIGNED(addr))\n\t\treturn -EINVAL;\n\n\tret \u003d __pkvm_host_donate_hyp(hyp_virt_to_pfn(addr), 1);\n\tif (ret)\n\t\treturn ret;\n\n\tmemset(addr, 0, PAGE_SIZE);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n```\n\njust to make it more explicit. But with `__get_free_page(GFP_ATOMIC | __GFP_ZERO);` we have it for \"free`. However I leave the decision to you. \n\nWhereas when comes to `its_shadow_tables` it might make sense to check the alignment, because we are not GIC owners and a potential regression might easily go unnoticed.",
